WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:17.827 --> 01:19.496
The strongest wind is one

01:20.371 --> 01:22.916
that blows within one's fist-sized heart.

01:23.875 --> 01:25.877
Nothing could withstand such wind.

01:26.795 --> 01:28.254
I'm completely innocent.

01:29.547 --> 01:31.382
Looking up at the sky, I have…

01:33.760 --> 01:34.886
no shame, you know.

01:36.471 --> 01:37.472
So why?

01:39.099 --> 01:42.560
Why am I no longer chief
and just put out to pasture?

01:46.856 --> 01:48.191
Hey, Park Yeong-ran.

01:49.400 --> 01:50.401
Get over here.

01:57.992 --> 02:00.453
Are you ignoring me as well?

02:00.537 --> 02:02.122
I said get over here.

02:02.789 --> 02:04.666
What the heck do you do at home?

02:05.375 --> 02:09.754
You eat white rice with my money,
and you can't even handle one kid?

02:09.838 --> 02:11.714
That brat definitely takes after you.

02:11.798 --> 02:13.133
I know everything!

02:13.216 --> 02:14.759
Just sleep if you're drunk!

02:15.927 --> 02:18.096
What was that, punk?
Whose kid are you anyway?

02:18.680 --> 02:21.182
-Whose side are you on?
-Father, do you even know how old I am?

02:30.191 --> 02:31.276
Hey!

02:31.359 --> 02:32.485
You punk!

02:32.569 --> 02:36.239
You never once came to my sports days.
Maybe you never saw me as your kid.

02:36.322 --> 02:39.784
When you're fooling around enjoying
spring flowers and snowy mountains…

02:39.868 --> 02:41.369
"Fooling around"?

02:41.452 --> 02:43.580
Mom never missed a day
packing us a hot lunch.

02:43.663 --> 02:44.998
Hey!

02:45.790 --> 02:48.668
Who brought your new mother
into this house, huh?

02:49.544 --> 02:51.880
Your stepmom can be replaced anytime,

02:51.963 --> 02:54.340
but you and I are family by blood!

02:54.424 --> 02:57.552
-If you two split up, I'm going with Mom.
-What was that, punk?

02:57.635 --> 03:02.682
I'm only treating you like a father
because Mom lives with you.

03:04.893 --> 03:06.144
Fetch the broom.

03:07.896 --> 03:09.230
Where's the broom, huh?

03:11.107 --> 03:12.734
Oh-seong, go to your room.

03:14.027 --> 03:15.403
You shouldn't talk like that.

03:15.486 --> 03:18.406
Split up with him!
What are you holding onto?

03:18.489 --> 03:21.659
I'm going to stay with your father.

03:22.702 --> 03:23.953
I'm staying with him.

03:28.833 --> 03:30.126
Darn it!

03:38.593 --> 03:39.719
That's right!

03:40.220 --> 03:43.056
You'd never survive without me.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.476
You all eat well, thanks to my money.

03:47.810 --> 03:48.645
Don't you?

03:49.729 --> 03:51.397
You even eat white rice!

03:52.899 --> 03:54.108
I have to stay.

03:57.946 --> 03:59.072
I have to live with him.

03:59.155 --> 04:00.740
Goddamn it!

04:01.699 --> 04:03.368
I'll spend the rest of my life with him

04:05.078 --> 04:08.456
and see how it all ends.

04:16.464 --> 04:19.175
KNOCK
YOU BETTER KNOCK

04:45.535 --> 04:46.369
Get out.

04:49.205 --> 04:50.540
You little…

04:52.709 --> 04:55.086
I wish I could knock you out
with a flying kick.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.671
I said get out!

04:56.754 --> 04:57.588
Seriously.

04:58.214 --> 04:59.215
Oh man.

05:02.302 --> 05:04.053
Mom!

05:04.137 --> 05:07.849
I'd have given you a beating
if you were Han-eum. You know that?

05:08.641 --> 05:11.311
You look like an army sergeant,
and you're dating?

05:11.978 --> 05:14.397
Why do you even have
this actress's picture?

05:14.480 --> 05:16.691
You'd need to be born again
to look like her.

05:16.774 --> 05:18.568
Get out of my room!

05:18.651 --> 05:21.195
How are you involved
with that family's son?

05:21.279 --> 05:23.614
You fool. You know, his mother and our…

05:25.491 --> 05:27.702
-Damn it.
-What about his mom?

05:28.494 --> 05:30.204
You guys won't work out anyway.

05:30.913 --> 05:32.749
You'll be mortified later.

05:32.832 --> 05:35.501
Stop this bullshit
while I'm still being nice.

05:37.920 --> 05:39.297
Why won't we work out anyway?

05:43.468 --> 05:44.677
Go tell him…

05:48.431 --> 05:50.266
I will kill him if I ever see him.

05:57.190 --> 05:58.232
Let's just break up.

05:59.067 --> 06:01.694
No, I don't want to! Why?

06:02.487 --> 06:04.655
Because of those bastards
Oh-seong and Han-eum?

06:04.739 --> 06:06.366
Or because of my father?

06:06.866 --> 06:09.202
My father is my father, but I'm me.

06:09.285 --> 06:11.245
I never listen to him anyway.

06:11.871 --> 06:15.708
Listen, don't go around
saying you're my girlfriend anymore.

06:16.292 --> 06:19.295
Don't cut in line at the cafeteria
thinking I've got your back.

06:20.797 --> 06:23.132
Only go to the roller rink in Ssangbong.

06:23.633 --> 06:25.426
No, I'm still gonna do it.

06:25.510 --> 06:28.137
You can't date anyone but me anyway.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.681
If you do, I'll beat them up.

06:30.765 --> 06:32.183
You think I won't?

06:32.266 --> 06:33.935
You think I won't?

06:34.894 --> 06:35.895
I think you will.

06:36.521 --> 06:38.731
No, I can't break up with you.

06:38.815 --> 06:40.316
I won't.

06:41.776 --> 06:44.195
-One last thing, Bu Hyeon-suk.
-What?

06:51.285 --> 06:52.328
Stay healthy.

07:00.002 --> 07:00.837
They're crying.

07:04.298 --> 07:05.675
You son of a bitch!

07:08.010 --> 07:10.721
Don't ever let me see you again.

07:10.805 --> 07:12.265
I will kill you!

07:14.016 --> 07:16.686
You're breaking up with me
just because you got beat up?

07:16.769 --> 07:19.272
I'll tell them to keep beating you up!

07:19.355 --> 07:20.898
Every single time they see you!

07:21.482 --> 07:23.067
You don't know how much it hurts!

07:25.236 --> 07:26.988
We can just run away from them.

07:27.071 --> 07:29.198
Make sure they don't catch you.

07:29.282 --> 07:32.869
The arcade, the roller rink, downtown.
I can't go anywhere.

07:33.619 --> 07:36.539
Your brothers' friends keep showing up.

07:36.622 --> 07:38.708
I got on the bus yesterday,

07:38.791 --> 07:41.169
and the driver was one of their friends.

07:42.545 --> 07:45.840
He told me not to get off the bus
until the last stop!

07:47.633 --> 07:50.136
Damn it! How can I keep living like this?

07:50.219 --> 07:52.221
I have my own life too.

07:53.556 --> 07:54.557
Then run away.

07:55.141 --> 07:56.517
Let's run away.

07:57.477 --> 08:00.021
-What?
-I can't live like this either.

08:00.104 --> 08:02.857
My father even removed my bedroom door.

08:04.984 --> 08:06.360
You want to run away?

08:06.444 --> 08:08.905
My dad said if I see you again,

08:08.988 --> 08:11.616
he'll shave my head
and send me to a Buddhist temple.

08:11.699 --> 08:12.742
You believe him?

08:13.451 --> 08:16.078
Then all your friends
would be Buddhist nuns by now.

08:17.830 --> 08:19.081
Do we run away or not?

08:23.169 --> 08:25.379
Are you going to run away or not?

08:26.464 --> 08:28.466
I don't know. Damn it!

08:38.100 --> 08:39.560
Keep honking.

08:40.269 --> 08:41.604
Keep honking the horn.

08:42.355 --> 08:43.648
Keep honking.

08:45.942 --> 08:48.402
Man, they look like
the center of the Korean flag.

08:49.362 --> 08:51.239
Come on. Those were the days!

08:51.322 --> 08:53.908
Apparently,
this is the spring of their lives.

08:53.991 --> 08:57.787
Is it because it's their spring,
or is it in their blood?

08:57.870 --> 08:59.163
I love you.

08:59.247 --> 09:00.790
I love you too.

09:00.873 --> 09:03.334
Looking back, spring was like a feast.

09:05.836 --> 09:07.380
Welcome home, son.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.840
But for the budding sprouts, it's a war.

09:09.924 --> 09:10.758
Hello.

09:12.260 --> 09:13.928
Do you frequent this place too?

09:14.804 --> 09:18.182
A trial for the new buds that push
their heads through the concrete.

09:28.609 --> 09:30.528
You can't even use the ladle properly.

09:33.281 --> 09:34.615
Your mom didn't teach you?

09:34.699 --> 09:37.660
It's just that the seaweed is all tangled.

09:38.244 --> 09:39.537
Don't use your hands!

09:40.621 --> 09:42.039
We don't do that in our family.

09:49.630 --> 09:51.007
You're really both here.

09:51.591 --> 09:53.134
This really is a happy birthday.

10:00.308 --> 10:02.685
Only one person was happy in that house.

10:16.073 --> 10:18.993
The kimchi tastes so good.

10:19.577 --> 10:21.579
Good kimchi is hard to find in Seoul.

10:21.662 --> 10:24.248
I mean, I'm not saying
all kimchi in Seoul is bad.

10:24.332 --> 10:25.333
I bought it.

10:30.254 --> 10:34.342
I haven't had a homemade meal in a while.
I feel like I can eat two bowls.

10:34.425 --> 10:35.593
We're light eaters.

10:40.264 --> 10:43.684
Do your parents know
you frequent a guy's apartment like this?

10:45.102 --> 10:48.439
She doesn't come over often.
It's my birthday, so I asked her to come.

10:49.774 --> 10:51.233
Did I ask you?

10:55.404 --> 10:56.322
Geum-myeong.

10:56.822 --> 11:00.117
This isn't Yeong-beom's apartment.
It's mine.

11:01.077 --> 11:02.453
An apartment I got for him.

11:03.454 --> 11:07.166
I don't want you frequenting my apartment.

11:08.084 --> 11:09.710
-Mother.
-It's my apartment.

11:10.336 --> 11:11.879
And I don't want you here.

11:14.590 --> 11:18.010
Sure, keep dating.
Learn how relationships work.

11:18.636 --> 11:21.013
I told you. I plan to marry Geum-myeong--

11:21.097 --> 11:22.014
Quiet.

11:24.975 --> 11:27.937
You wanted a place near your school,
and it was just for this…

11:31.148 --> 11:32.525
Just for this.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.570
You are my pride.

11:36.654 --> 11:38.572
Now my pride is bruised.

11:41.200 --> 11:44.203
Each had their heart rocked by love,

11:44.286 --> 11:47.081
and a storm swept through their heart.

11:47.164 --> 11:50.668
Does your family own a conglomerate?
Like Samsung or Hyundai?

11:50.751 --> 11:53.087
How much richer
could your family be than mine?

11:56.257 --> 11:59.552
We go to the same school,
and I'm just as precious to my parents.

11:59.635 --> 12:01.512
Why should I be ashamed
that I can't ladle soup?

12:01.595 --> 12:04.557
Are you better at it?
Did your mother teach you?

12:05.474 --> 12:06.976
I'm not good at ladling either.

12:08.144 --> 12:09.019
So unfair.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.524
I hate everything about this.

12:13.607 --> 12:16.819
I feel like I've become a cheap clown.

12:16.902 --> 12:19.697
I can't stand groveling
in front of a person

12:19.780 --> 12:22.616
who won't like me anyway,
no matter what I do.

12:23.117 --> 12:24.201
I hate it so much!

12:32.710 --> 12:33.878
DIGESTIVE DRINK

12:38.340 --> 12:39.967
Why did you eat so much?

12:40.843 --> 12:43.387
I wanted to impress her.

12:43.471 --> 12:45.347
Of course I did!

12:46.015 --> 12:49.101
Who wouldn't want to impress
her boyfriend's mother?

12:49.185 --> 12:52.772
Who would want to marry
the pride of his mother?

12:57.610 --> 12:58.778
Just choose one.

12:58.861 --> 13:01.906
Be a good son or a good husband.

13:02.406 --> 13:03.407
You can only be one.

13:03.991 --> 13:07.453
I don't want a man
who's just a little nice to everyone.

13:07.536 --> 13:10.748
Forget the proposal.
Choose one first before anything else.

13:11.457 --> 13:15.085
Well, who in the world
would choose one over the other?

13:15.586 --> 13:16.420
No man would--

13:16.504 --> 13:17.588
My dad.

13:18.339 --> 13:19.173
What?

13:19.715 --> 13:21.133
My dad did.

13:21.967 --> 13:22.802
I see.

13:24.428 --> 13:26.138
Let me make myself clear.

13:27.681 --> 13:29.809
I won't marry your mother's son.

13:31.894 --> 13:34.563
It was a time
when everything felt so sincere,

13:35.481 --> 13:39.318
like a little owl crying all night
at the slightest breeze.

13:41.862 --> 13:44.240
This is Kim Gi-deok on Two O'clock Date.

13:45.825 --> 13:50.621
I believe the '90s are truly
the renaissance of pop culture.

13:51.330 --> 13:53.123
The winds of change are here.

13:53.916 --> 13:55.835
I love this painting.

13:55.918 --> 13:57.753
I guess he won't be Picasso anymore.

13:57.837 --> 13:58.838
See?

13:58.921 --> 14:00.548
You can do your job properly.

14:00.631 --> 14:03.884
It's so obvious what the movie is about.

14:03.968 --> 14:07.638
Just looking at this
makes me want to do the Lambada.

14:09.557 --> 14:10.558
Great job!

14:13.435 --> 14:15.187
That lady's back again.

14:15.271 --> 14:17.690
She somehow always knows the release day.

14:18.607 --> 14:20.776
Where does she get the resale tickets?

14:20.860 --> 14:24.321
I've never sold her any tickets before.

14:24.405 --> 14:25.698
Maybe they're counterfeit?

14:51.765 --> 14:52.892
We don't want any.

14:53.642 --> 14:55.102
No, that's…

14:55.185 --> 14:57.187
-We don't want resale tickets.
-That's not…

14:59.023 --> 15:01.442
Does that look like Choi Jin-sil?

15:03.736 --> 15:06.113
Does it look like Choi Jin-sil?

15:06.196 --> 15:09.700
-I think it looks like her.
-It's a job well done, then.

15:10.200 --> 15:12.286
-Sorry?
-Or is it bad?

15:12.870 --> 15:14.330
No, I guess not.

15:14.413 --> 15:18.083
Apparently, it was painted
by a college art major.

15:18.876 --> 15:19.710
Right.

15:20.210 --> 15:23.380
Why do people go in without looking?
Is everyone busy or something?

15:23.464 --> 15:27.593
It makes me a little sad that people
don't even glance at the painting.

15:28.469 --> 15:29.637
It really does.

15:30.346 --> 15:33.390
A Picasso lived in the basement
of the Cannes Theater,

15:33.474 --> 15:36.060
and for someone,
this theater was their Louvre.

15:36.143 --> 15:38.938
Stop selling resale tickets!
I said stop it!

15:39.021 --> 15:41.482
Scalping is a nuisance to society!

15:42.066 --> 15:43.275
No resale tickets!

15:44.026 --> 15:45.569
I said no!

15:46.153 --> 15:48.364
Does he really think I'm a scalper?

16:05.422 --> 16:08.759
Since you're here,
it would be nice to watch a movie.

16:10.177 --> 16:12.638
I hear this movie
coming out in two days is great.

16:12.721 --> 16:14.598
It's being rereleased
due to its popularity.

16:17.309 --> 16:19.395
You shouldn't give out tickets to anyone.

16:19.478 --> 16:22.064
But you're not just anyone.

16:22.147 --> 16:25.943
This is an employee benefit
offered by the owner himself!

16:28.320 --> 16:30.906
Come at 2:00 p.m. on Monday.
It's normally empty then.

16:30.990 --> 16:32.950
It'll feel like you rented the theater.

16:34.201 --> 16:38.455
I'd prefer it if you didn't tell my son
I came here to see his paintings.

16:39.289 --> 16:41.375
Chung-seop doesn't know I come here.

16:41.458 --> 16:45.129
He leaves with his packed lunch
and comes home covered in paint.

16:45.212 --> 16:48.340
He never tells me what he paints or where.
He says he's embarrassed.

16:48.841 --> 16:51.010
Does just anyone get to paint
such big pictures?

16:51.093 --> 16:53.095
-If they paint, they're painters.
-Of course.

16:53.178 --> 16:55.889
He painted that so well.
I'm just dying to see what he does.

17:00.102 --> 17:03.188
I've seen everything Chung-seop
has painted since elementary school.

17:03.272 --> 17:04.523
That's been my joy.

17:05.816 --> 17:08.027
These days, movie release days are my joy.

17:09.361 --> 17:10.487
PROMOTIONAL TICKET

17:10.571 --> 17:13.449
Our theater would be ruined
without Artist Park.

17:20.080 --> 17:22.332
Sir, you're not from Seoul, are you?

17:23.333 --> 17:24.251
Honestly.

17:27.379 --> 17:28.881
-Wow.
-Wow!

17:39.933 --> 17:41.477
What is it this time?

17:41.560 --> 17:44.438
Did Eun-myeong sell something
at school again?

17:46.231 --> 17:47.274
Eun-myeong's mom.

17:47.858 --> 17:49.985
Don't call me that from now on.

17:50.069 --> 17:52.696
Should we just call you Geum-myeong's mom?

17:54.156 --> 17:55.532
No calls from Seoul?

17:55.616 --> 17:57.326
Geum-myeong has a boyfriend, I swear.

17:57.409 --> 17:59.411
She's forgotten Mom and Dad already.

17:59.995 --> 18:01.830
Goodness me. It's so unfair.

18:01.914 --> 18:05.042
It's as if she's doing us a favor
by calling us first.

18:05.834 --> 18:08.253
They are only children
when they're in your arms.

18:08.337 --> 18:11.465
Once they leave,
they're busier than the president.

18:11.548 --> 18:14.384
My children are
the busiest people in the world.

18:15.385 --> 18:17.596
What, did you have another bad dream?

18:27.898 --> 18:31.944
Why did the school call you this time?
Is he bottom of his class again?

18:32.027 --> 18:33.862
He's never bottom of his class.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.614
Cheol-yong is in that class.

18:38.283 --> 18:39.868
It's about cigarettes.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.538
You said you wouldn't tell.

18:42.621 --> 18:44.915
Does that little punk smoke?

18:44.998 --> 18:46.083
He doesn't smoke!

18:46.750 --> 18:47.876
He sold them.

18:48.585 --> 18:51.672
-He sold cigarettes.
-Wow.

18:51.755 --> 18:53.340
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

18:53.423 --> 18:54.925
He really is something.

18:55.008 --> 18:58.303
Isn't the seller more impressive
than the smoker?

18:58.387 --> 19:03.225
He lied to the old man at the variety shop
about the cigarettes being for us,

19:03.308 --> 19:06.728
then bought them
and basically made a delivery.

19:06.812 --> 19:09.022
They say he sold them at a markup.

19:09.690 --> 19:12.693
Personally, I'm more curious
about what Eun-myeong will become

19:12.776 --> 19:13.944
than Geum-myeong.

19:16.780 --> 19:18.824
Have you asked why he does it?

19:18.907 --> 19:20.450
What do you mean "why"?

19:21.160 --> 19:23.996
He's just an angsty teenager
acting entitled.

19:24.079 --> 19:28.709
I mean, have you ever asked
why he desperately needs money?

19:30.377 --> 19:33.005
I don't know why he's obsessed with money!

19:33.505 --> 19:35.757
That's why you should ask.

19:35.841 --> 19:38.343
You gave birth to his body, not his mind.

19:38.886 --> 19:42.055
You know,
you're helpless with Geum-myeong,

19:42.139 --> 19:44.808
but a boss to Eun-myeong.

19:44.892 --> 19:49.771
You handle picky Geum-myeong
like soft tofu,

19:49.855 --> 19:53.192
and easygoing Eun-myeong
like a radish being tossed around.

19:53.275 --> 19:56.820
Geum-myeong takes after me
and is a bit emotionally sensitive,

19:56.904 --> 19:59.573
and Eun-myeong is, you know--

19:59.656 --> 20:00.616
A pushover?

20:00.699 --> 20:01.700
I don't think that!

20:02.951 --> 20:06.538
A radish may look fine
no matter how many times it falls,

20:06.622 --> 20:09.750
but even the sturdiest radish
can crack inside.

20:10.751 --> 20:13.921
Don't treat your children differently.

20:14.880 --> 20:18.258
Children… remember everything.

20:18.342 --> 20:20.969
It's because I'm upset too.

20:21.845 --> 20:25.265
I can't help but get more mad
about the one I worry about the most.

20:26.141 --> 20:28.060
So it has nothing to do

20:28.143 --> 20:31.104
with Geum-myeong making you proud
and Eun-myeong embarrassing you?

20:31.855 --> 20:34.233
So what if it does? Am I a saint?

20:35.108 --> 20:37.527
What could I possibly do?

20:40.364 --> 20:43.325
…may be the star of tomorrow.

20:43.825 --> 20:46.078
A choice ahead of its time.

20:46.161 --> 20:48.455
High-performance Elantra.

21:02.719 --> 21:03.553
So…

21:05.347 --> 21:08.600
I'm in your debt once again.
I don't know how I'll repay you.

21:09.977 --> 21:11.436
There's no need.

21:12.354 --> 21:14.898
But I'd still like to…

21:20.612 --> 21:23.949
Then could you paint something for me
when you have time?

21:24.032 --> 21:26.118
So I can sell it for a high price someday.

21:26.702 --> 21:29.705
I heard Picasso's work
became more valuable after he died.

21:30.622 --> 21:34.710
But there's no guarantee I'll die first…

21:40.841 --> 21:42.467
-Was that a joke?
-Yeah.

21:47.055 --> 21:49.141
-I should go back to the box office.
-Well…

21:51.226 --> 21:52.060
What is it?

21:54.104 --> 21:55.063
Thank you, really.

21:55.147 --> 21:57.858
There's no need.
I didn't spend my own money or anything.

21:57.941 --> 22:00.402
No, I mean, my mother…

22:06.742 --> 22:08.994
It's her first time
seeing a movie in a theater.

22:17.669 --> 22:19.171
Mister! You have to run.

22:19.796 --> 22:21.590
Oh no, you have to run!

22:31.641 --> 22:34.603
Even though she watches
The Weekend Classic Movie every week.

22:35.228 --> 22:36.063
I guess

22:37.272 --> 22:39.107
I'd been so focused on my own life.

22:46.865 --> 22:50.369
Each person was swayed
by the love in their heart.

22:50.911 --> 22:51.995
You know what?

22:52.746 --> 22:55.749
I started crying when the projectionist
walked in with shades on.

22:56.249 --> 22:57.084
Alfredo?

22:58.210 --> 23:00.921
Why wasn't there a fire extinguisher
in the projection room?

23:01.004 --> 23:03.298
Why put out the fire?
He should've saved himself.

23:03.382 --> 23:05.133
He should've jumped out the window.

23:05.217 --> 23:07.469
Then he would've only broken his legs.

23:09.221 --> 23:11.932
I wonder what he did
after losing his projectionist job.

23:12.516 --> 23:15.435
Maybe Toto sent him money
because he's kind.

23:15.519 --> 23:18.063
Did you cry because
you thought Alfredo might be broke?

23:18.980 --> 23:20.190
You know, Toto

23:21.983 --> 23:23.068
reminds me of you.

23:26.405 --> 23:27.697
Toto is like my son.

23:29.950 --> 23:31.952
What did you want to give to Ms. Yang?

23:32.452 --> 23:33.662
I'll give it to her.

23:34.955 --> 23:36.706
Did you say you're an English major?

23:37.791 --> 23:38.625
Yes.

23:39.126 --> 23:40.877
PHOTOCOPY, PRINTING, BINDING

23:40.961 --> 23:44.005
You can rely on me until you graduate.

23:45.799 --> 23:48.802
These are all in English.
People just won't pick them up.

23:49.302 --> 23:51.513
It'd cost a fortune to buy them all.

23:51.596 --> 23:53.682
English ones are even more expensive.

23:53.765 --> 23:55.684
There are some study notes in here too.

23:56.184 --> 23:59.688
I'm not sure if I can accept all of these.

24:00.397 --> 24:02.149
So this is why parents love daughters.

24:02.232 --> 24:06.069
I'm here all the time,
so every day feels the same.

24:06.153 --> 24:09.322
The only special thing I did
was to see new paintings on premiere days.

24:09.406 --> 24:12.367
But I was truly happy today,
thanks to you, Ms. Yang.

24:12.951 --> 24:17.038
I think I'll remember this day
until I draw my last breath.

24:20.542 --> 24:22.461
Hearing you say that

24:22.544 --> 24:23.962
makes me feel like

24:25.130 --> 24:28.341
I've done something extraordinary.

24:29.009 --> 24:30.760
Mother, that's enough.

24:31.344 --> 24:33.221
How can she carry them all?

24:33.889 --> 24:35.265
She can't carry them alone.

24:37.601 --> 24:38.643
She can't.

25:05.879 --> 25:07.088
How about a drink?

25:07.964 --> 25:10.383
Well, a drink…

25:10.967 --> 25:12.677
-Maybe we shouldn't?
-Here you are.

25:13.261 --> 25:15.096
Yeah, that's a bit…

25:16.306 --> 25:17.307
All right, then.

25:23.271 --> 25:24.272
You know…

25:26.525 --> 25:27.359
Yes?

25:27.442 --> 25:28.443
If you're grateful,

25:28.527 --> 25:31.154
maybe clear my name
instead of buying noodles?

25:33.907 --> 25:38.245
The landlord's daughter
keeps kicking my shoes outside my door.

25:40.163 --> 25:42.791
She knows that there's nothing between us.

25:43.750 --> 25:44.960
I guess

25:46.169 --> 25:48.296
she wants to get married
without feeling guilty.

25:50.215 --> 25:53.885
So you're sending off your girlfriend
to marry someone else?

25:56.304 --> 25:57.764
You must have

25:58.473 --> 25:59.516
a really big heart.

26:01.476 --> 26:03.603
She's marrying
the son of a noodle shop owner.

26:03.687 --> 26:05.647
Do they make a fortune selling noodles?

26:06.439 --> 26:07.774
The Pildong Noodles chain.

26:12.195 --> 26:14.531
It's a perfect family to marry into,

26:15.490 --> 26:16.491
but she can't

26:18.159 --> 26:19.369
bring herself to do it.

26:20.662 --> 26:21.955
Then just hold onto her.

26:22.581 --> 26:26.376
It's her fate if she dumps Picasso
and goes to the noodle guy.

26:26.459 --> 26:28.086
Tell her to her face,

26:28.587 --> 26:31.631
"Leave if you want.
It's your loss, not mine."

26:33.508 --> 26:37.512
You should bring a gift and say,
"Please let me marry your daughter."

26:37.596 --> 26:40.390
That way,
at least you won't have any regrets.

26:40.473 --> 26:43.101
How would you know
if I'm better than the noodle guy?

26:43.768 --> 26:46.021
You don't know me very well.

26:46.104 --> 26:47.939
You're really precious to your mom.

26:52.360 --> 26:55.196
That's why you paint everything
however you please.

26:56.114 --> 26:58.950
That's just deeply rooted guts, you know?

27:01.536 --> 27:03.371
I'm precious to my parents too.

27:04.497 --> 27:05.665
I'd just like to think

27:05.749 --> 27:08.084
that holding my head high
and living my life

27:08.877 --> 27:11.004
is what keeps my folks' pride intact.

27:12.005 --> 27:14.424
At least I'd like to think so.

27:18.845 --> 27:23.141
You know, you don't need to take sides
with someone you barely know.

27:23.224 --> 27:24.851
It's not like I don't know.

27:25.352 --> 27:27.187
People are the same, after all.

27:27.270 --> 27:28.647
No, they are different.

27:29.439 --> 27:32.525
Everyone has a dark side, after all.

27:36.363 --> 27:39.616
It was a time
when strangers were dangerous,

27:39.699 --> 27:41.701
and kindness from a stranger
was dangerous.

27:41.785 --> 27:46.331
Less than three months after a 13-year-old
was killed in the Hwaseong serial murders…

27:46.414 --> 27:49.501
Oh my. I'm so sorry again.

27:50.794 --> 27:53.463
Yes, please let me know. Please.

27:54.130 --> 27:56.049
Those bastards should be beaten to death!

27:56.132 --> 27:58.718
The phrase "beaten to death"
exists for a reason.

27:58.802 --> 28:00.136
How bad must they be?

28:00.220 --> 28:03.181
Is that right? Okay, I see.

28:03.848 --> 28:05.767
When Geum-myeoung gets back,

28:06.434 --> 28:08.978
could you please ask her to call--

28:10.188 --> 28:12.899
Yes, okay. Thank you.

28:13.817 --> 28:15.485
When you kidnap a child,

28:15.568 --> 28:18.780
you're taking three lives, not just one.

28:18.863 --> 28:21.449
How can parents cope with losing a child?

28:27.956 --> 28:31.459
I mean, losing a child
is devastating in itself,

28:31.543 --> 28:33.545
but to lose your child like that…

28:34.045 --> 28:34.879
Goodness me.

28:37.507 --> 28:40.051
Why? Is Geum-myeong out late again?

28:40.802 --> 28:43.138
I don't understand
why she's out so late at night.

28:43.722 --> 28:45.306
I told her to stay home at night.

28:45.807 --> 28:48.101
What's wrong?
Do you keep having bad dreams?

28:48.852 --> 28:49.686
About what?

28:53.648 --> 28:57.110
Maybe you feel that way
because the ancestral rite has come up.

28:57.694 --> 29:00.697
Something odd happened to you
at an ancestral rite as a child.

29:00.780 --> 29:01.614
On Aegi Hill?

29:02.532 --> 29:04.492
We were there together, right?

29:05.118 --> 29:07.996
Goodness, just thinking about it
gives me the chills.

29:09.873 --> 29:13.918
I can still remember the smells
from that day.

29:47.869 --> 29:50.914
Hurry! They put meat
on the ancestral rite table.

29:50.997 --> 29:53.541
My father will give it all to my brother.

29:53.625 --> 29:56.753
Only people can see that black dragonfly.

29:56.836 --> 29:59.088
They say other dragonflies can't see it.

29:59.172 --> 30:00.006
Why not?

30:00.089 --> 30:02.425
Because it's the Grim Reaper
of dragonflies.

30:04.552 --> 30:08.515
We humans can't see
the Grim Reaper either, you know.

30:14.229 --> 30:15.980
What is it? Are you going to catch it?

30:16.564 --> 30:17.816
You go ahead.

30:18.441 --> 30:20.151
Let's just go!

30:21.027 --> 30:22.278
If I catch it,

30:22.821 --> 30:25.240
it won't be able to take
the other dragonflies.

30:25.323 --> 30:29.744
Baby dragonflies would want to live
with their mom and dad too.

30:29.828 --> 30:31.996
Father is going to scold you again.

30:32.956 --> 30:35.375
Is that what people call being possessed?

30:35.959 --> 30:37.418
I don't know why I chased it.

30:59.524 --> 31:03.778
AEGI HILL
BUS STOP

31:17.834 --> 31:21.045
I need to take the bus, but my legs hurt.

31:23.131 --> 31:24.674
Could you go to the store

31:25.383 --> 31:27.594
to exchange this for ten-hwan coins?

31:41.900 --> 31:43.610
What did the store owner say?

31:44.360 --> 31:46.154
That it's not his job to change coins.

31:47.405 --> 31:49.324
-Did he scold you?
-No.

31:49.949 --> 31:51.784
But he did give me a side-eye.

31:53.494 --> 31:54.495
For your trouble.

31:59.709 --> 32:02.503
You're really kind and so gentle.

32:04.172 --> 32:05.965
You listen well, don't you?

32:06.049 --> 32:06.883
But

32:07.926 --> 32:09.969
you don't have to give me this.

32:10.053 --> 32:11.930
Then, can you do it once more?

32:12.513 --> 32:14.474
I need to take two buses.

32:20.605 --> 32:23.149
Since the store owner
didn't like giving change,

32:24.150 --> 32:28.655
you can find the cabbage truck vendor
in the alley behind the telephone pole.

32:29.781 --> 32:31.866
Could you get some change from that man?

32:32.367 --> 32:34.994
Then I'll give you another one.

32:37.497 --> 32:39.499
It's just that my legs hurt.

33:12.740 --> 33:14.367
What are you doing here?

33:14.450 --> 33:16.577
-Mom.
-What are you doing?

33:17.453 --> 33:19.664
-What about you, Mom?
-What's this money?

33:23.001 --> 33:25.920
-Mister!
-What? You know that man?

33:35.805 --> 33:38.558
That lady was just here.

33:39.726 --> 33:42.020
Gwang-rye said her heart was pounding,

33:42.520 --> 33:45.023
but she said nothing
so she wouldn't scare you.

33:45.815 --> 33:47.775
But, Mom, what are you doing here?

33:50.069 --> 33:51.904
It was such an odd coincidence.

33:52.405 --> 33:55.742
I was in a neighborhood I'd never been to,

33:55.825 --> 34:00.204
and I ran into my mom,
who would never go there.

34:00.705 --> 34:02.373
You still don't know, do you?

34:02.874 --> 34:05.543
Your mother went out
to look for you that day.

34:12.258 --> 34:14.635
I don't need to get firewood,
thanks to you, Sister.

34:14.719 --> 34:16.095
Don't call her sister anymore.

34:16.596 --> 34:18.681
We still have the firewood
you brought before.

34:19.432 --> 34:21.142
It's the least she can do.

34:21.225 --> 34:26.147
Her child has been living and eating here
for free for years now.

34:26.230 --> 34:28.483
She should at least do that
for child support.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.903
Don't make Ae-sun carry wood.

34:32.904 --> 34:34.822
Replace the jeongjong with makgeolli.

34:35.323 --> 34:37.033
Han-gyu likes makgeolli better.

34:39.202 --> 34:40.203
Where's Ae-sun?

34:40.953 --> 34:45.208
It's her father's ancestral rite,
but all she cares about is going out.

34:45.291 --> 34:48.586
Where's Ae-sun?
There's meat soup. Where is she?

34:50.630 --> 34:52.465
She went after a Grim Reaper dragonfly.

34:53.257 --> 34:54.217
What?

34:55.218 --> 34:57.512
A mother's instinct is a scary thing.

34:58.012 --> 35:00.431
Apparently, she ran over a mountain
in no time.

35:05.645 --> 35:07.688
You should be the one
eating Dad's meat soup.

35:08.189 --> 35:10.191
Why wander around instead?

35:17.240 --> 35:18.241
Give it to me.

35:18.741 --> 35:21.285
Why? This one is mine.

35:21.828 --> 35:22.662
It's bad luck.

35:37.301 --> 35:40.096
How did you know I was here?

35:40.596 --> 35:44.183
I have eyes in the back of my head.
That's what it takes to be a mom.

35:47.061 --> 35:49.564
Do you think she'll come to get her money?

35:52.650 --> 35:53.943
-Ae-sun.
-Yes?

35:54.026 --> 35:55.653
Did she see your face?

35:56.612 --> 35:57.446
Yes.

35:58.698 --> 36:00.825
What did she look like?

36:02.743 --> 36:06.622
She had a pale face,
and on her wrist, something strange…

36:06.706 --> 36:09.917
You think your mom would let someone off
for messing with her child?

36:16.299 --> 36:18.718
Here, check it out!

36:19.302 --> 36:21.971
Come see! We'll give you the best.
Fresh from the haenyeo!

36:22.054 --> 36:24.390
Three for 50 hwan. Here you go.

36:24.473 --> 36:25.892
I don't care.

36:25.975 --> 36:27.268
Just give me one more.

36:27.351 --> 36:30.479
Come on,
we put our lives on the line for these.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.190
Forget it, then.

36:32.273 --> 36:33.107
Goodness me!

36:34.192 --> 36:35.484
My goodness!

36:38.362 --> 36:41.699
Hey! Are you going to check the wrist
of every woman in Jeju?

36:41.782 --> 36:42.783
Seriously!

36:47.038 --> 36:50.499
You're driving all our customers away
by yanking their wrists.

36:50.583 --> 36:53.044
Are you selling conches
to catch the culprit?

36:53.127 --> 36:55.838
That bitch saw Ae-sun's face.

36:57.381 --> 36:58.883
I'm going to buy some conches.

36:59.675 --> 37:00.927
They're practically free!

37:01.969 --> 37:03.054
What's your price?

37:05.389 --> 37:06.641
What's your offer?

37:08.851 --> 37:10.394
Hey, I sent the boat back.

37:11.312 --> 37:13.564
Why do you always go after the young ones?

37:13.648 --> 37:15.650
Is there an age limit for begging?

37:18.319 --> 37:19.987
You touch it, you buy it. Okay?

37:21.822 --> 37:26.035
They don't listen as they get older.
Kind kids who are so gentle are the best.

37:27.161 --> 37:29.121
That girl was just perfect.

37:30.039 --> 37:30.873
What the hell?

37:31.374 --> 37:32.458
-What is it?
-Come on!

37:32.541 --> 37:34.877
Let's make a sale
before you yank her wrist!

37:34.961 --> 37:36.254
You must've lost your mind.

37:36.921 --> 37:38.923
Are you out of your mind? Let her go!

37:41.509 --> 37:43.552
What the hell? How are you so strong?

37:43.636 --> 37:45.346
You should be beaten to death, bitch!

37:45.429 --> 37:48.224
You were going to make my daughter
beg for money?

37:53.104 --> 37:57.441
These scumbags! Get that bastard!
They need to be beaten to death!

38:02.029 --> 38:04.740
You bastard, get over here!

38:05.825 --> 38:06.826
You bitch!

38:11.122 --> 38:11.956
So what happened?

38:12.039 --> 38:16.210
There were no open endings
in fairy tales back then.

38:16.794 --> 38:18.462
She beat her to death. Obviously.

38:19.046 --> 38:21.257
She beat her to death?

38:21.340 --> 38:24.635
Those scumbags deserved
to be beaten to death, didn't they?

38:24.719 --> 38:27.054
Don't ever come back here, you bastard!

38:27.138 --> 38:28.472
Die, you bitch!

38:43.696 --> 38:47.241
At the time, the country didn't have
much of a legal system,

38:48.075 --> 38:52.705
so the police didn't say much
if you beat up those who deserved it.

38:53.706 --> 38:55.791
Even if you left someone half-dead,

38:56.375 --> 38:59.587
the cops would clean up the mess
and take them away.

38:59.670 --> 39:01.922
The cops themselves
used to beat people up.

39:03.841 --> 39:06.510
It happened to be the day
of Han-gyu's ancestral rite.

39:07.887 --> 39:11.223
Your mom said that your father saved you.

39:11.307 --> 39:12.558
But I don't think so.

39:12.641 --> 39:15.519
It was your mom who saved her child.

39:15.603 --> 39:17.605
Nothing beats a mother's instinct.

39:19.273 --> 39:20.149
Oh dear.

39:20.232 --> 39:22.401
Mother wakes up this late.

39:23.027 --> 39:24.862
She may forget everything else,

39:24.945 --> 39:27.531
but she never forgets
the day her eldest son visits.

39:28.949 --> 39:30.951
Nothing beats a mother's instinct.

39:31.660 --> 39:34.955
My mom told me back then

39:36.749 --> 39:38.876
that you need eyes
in the back of your head

39:39.377 --> 39:40.878
to be a mother.

39:51.472 --> 39:53.641
Hey, you have a call.

39:54.141 --> 39:54.975
Okay.

39:58.521 --> 40:00.189
For goodness' sake.

40:00.272 --> 40:03.275
Do people in Jeju not watch Eyes of Dawn?

40:03.359 --> 40:05.653
She always calls when this show is on.

40:06.153 --> 40:08.739
Yeah, everything's fine.

40:10.116 --> 40:12.201
What could possibly happen
in just one day?

40:13.244 --> 40:15.162
EYES OF DAWN

40:16.580 --> 40:19.083
Are you going to call me
every time you have a dream?

40:19.166 --> 40:23.129
Why are you always home late these days?
Where do you go wandering every night?

40:23.212 --> 40:24.463
I don't go wandering.

40:25.047 --> 40:27.716
Did they fix the light in your alley?

40:27.800 --> 40:30.803
It's a scary world out there.
Be home early.

40:30.886 --> 40:32.555
Make sure you sleep at home.

40:32.638 --> 40:35.224
No staying out overnight.
I'll know if you do.

40:35.307 --> 40:37.726
Do you call every night
to see if I'm only having fun?

40:38.227 --> 40:40.771
You're not seeing anyone, are you?

40:41.564 --> 40:43.774
I won't be able to handle it
if you upset me too.

40:44.358 --> 40:46.694
You are your mom and dad's pride.

40:46.777 --> 40:49.822
All my hope is in you,
so if the pillar starts acting up--

40:49.905 --> 40:51.157
That damn pillar…

40:53.951 --> 40:55.578
Am I everything in your life?

40:55.661 --> 40:59.081
Don't you have a life of your own?
Think about it.

40:59.165 --> 41:02.251
Even if I stay out all night,
you can't do anything from there.

41:02.334 --> 41:05.504
If I wanted to fool you,
I could do it 100 or 1,000 times.

41:05.588 --> 41:06.589
Good for you.

41:06.672 --> 41:10.634
So stop fussing over it, please.

41:11.177 --> 41:13.012
You need to live your own life.

41:13.554 --> 41:14.805
Wait until you have a kid.

41:14.889 --> 41:18.225
Wait until you have a daughter
just like you!

41:20.227 --> 41:22.897
You wear these hairpins every day
and lose them every day.

41:23.397 --> 41:26.192
Why do I bother buying them for you?
You lose them every day.

41:27.610 --> 41:29.361
She thinks she's the only great one.

41:31.697 --> 41:34.992
I saw this at the hardware store,
so I bought one.

41:38.037 --> 41:40.080
Visit her in Seoul
and install it yourself.

41:41.081 --> 41:44.084
I'm sure she can do it herself
since she's so great.

41:44.710 --> 41:46.837
I'm the only fool for making a fuss.

41:47.755 --> 41:50.174
They are only children
when they're in your arms.

41:52.510 --> 41:54.470
She's the one growing up, not me.

41:54.553 --> 41:56.805
My heart is still the same.

41:58.182 --> 41:59.808
Is this about that dream?

42:02.144 --> 42:04.271
What is this dream you keep having?

42:06.899 --> 42:10.027
Why won't you say anything?
Is the dream that bad these days?

42:10.945 --> 42:12.238
It's not a bad dream.

42:12.988 --> 42:14.114
It's nothing much.

42:44.687 --> 42:45.688
Mom!

42:56.240 --> 42:57.408
Mom!

43:02.162 --> 43:03.414
Mom.

43:22.182 --> 43:25.728
I told you I'd give you candy
after you finish your sujebi, didn't I?

43:25.811 --> 43:27.646
Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

43:27.730 --> 43:28.897
Mommy, give me a hug.

43:31.984 --> 43:34.320
Ms. Oh! Geum-myeong was in an accident!

43:34.403 --> 43:36.280
Is she bleeding?

43:54.173 --> 43:57.926
I told you I'd give you candy
after you finish your sujebi, didn't I?

43:58.010 --> 43:59.803
Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

44:07.519 --> 44:08.437
Another bad dream?

44:10.147 --> 44:11.148
Oh dear.

44:14.818 --> 44:17.279
What dreams have you been having lately?

44:20.908 --> 44:23.285
…I'd give you candy
after you finish your sujebi.

44:23.369 --> 44:25.329
Ms. Oh! Geum-myeong was in an accident!

44:25.412 --> 44:26.372
Is she bleeding?

45:47.578 --> 45:48.412
Baby.

45:51.498 --> 45:52.458
Mommy…

45:54.710 --> 45:56.920
is going to get your sister
and come right back.

45:58.464 --> 45:59.298
Okay?

46:03.635 --> 46:05.012
I'll go get her.

46:11.351 --> 46:12.686
When I get back,

46:13.896 --> 46:15.689
I'll give you candy every day.

46:16.648 --> 46:17.483
Okay?

46:21.528 --> 46:23.363
Mom, by mere coincidence,

46:24.239 --> 46:26.742
has lost immeasurable things.

46:33.832 --> 46:35.584
That's why she fussed even more,

46:36.835 --> 46:40.756
believing that restless worry
could prevent even coincidences.

46:41.256 --> 46:43.008
Geum-myeong.

46:48.472 --> 46:49.473
Baby.

46:50.432 --> 46:51.266
Baby.

46:52.267 --> 46:53.101
Baby.

46:54.061 --> 46:55.813
Baby!

47:05.030 --> 47:06.532
Oh no. Good heavens.

47:07.825 --> 47:10.744
My baby. Oh my God.

47:13.914 --> 47:14.748
Help!

47:16.542 --> 47:17.417
Help!

47:18.126 --> 47:19.837
Baby.

47:20.504 --> 47:21.547
What's wrong with him?

47:23.090 --> 47:24.049
Baby.

47:25.300 --> 47:26.301
The doctor.

47:27.427 --> 47:29.346
We need to call the doctor.

47:34.101 --> 47:35.102
An ambulance.

47:35.185 --> 47:37.604
An ambulance. Call an…

47:39.523 --> 47:42.568
Gwan-sik, call an ambulance.

47:42.651 --> 47:45.070
Why won't anyone call the ambulance?

47:49.533 --> 47:52.202
Geum-myeong.

48:07.342 --> 48:08.343
Help!

48:09.386 --> 48:11.847
Help! Ambulance!

48:12.347 --> 48:14.308
Someone, call an ambulance!

48:14.391 --> 48:16.351
Ambulance!

48:18.020 --> 48:18.896
Baby!

48:45.339 --> 48:48.467
Look, you can't just be walking
through there like this…

48:48.550 --> 48:49.384
What?

48:49.468 --> 48:52.679
She's inhaled coal gas!

48:53.639 --> 48:54.681
What? Oh no!

48:55.432 --> 48:59.645
San-108, Bongcheon 5-dong.

48:59.728 --> 49:00.938
108!

49:01.647 --> 49:03.357
108! Yes!

49:04.232 --> 49:06.735
No, there are stairs here!

49:06.818 --> 49:08.195
You can't drive up here.

49:08.278 --> 49:09.112
Yes.

49:15.410 --> 49:18.121
It was a time
when genuine kindness froze over…

49:18.205 --> 49:19.623
Oh no.

49:20.832 --> 49:22.668
Baby, Mom's here.

49:22.751 --> 49:23.835
Mom's right here.

49:25.212 --> 49:28.590
…the year Korea's three major
unsolved cases occurred,

49:29.132 --> 49:32.594
Mom called me every night
after the nine o'clock news.

49:33.095 --> 49:34.346
Here, we're over here!

49:35.097 --> 49:36.848
Her relentless worry was tiresome.

49:36.932 --> 49:39.309
Sir! Please help us!

49:39.393 --> 49:43.814
But… it was the same relentless worry
that saved me again.

49:50.570 --> 49:52.239
Why is it so quiet?

50:00.831 --> 50:01.790
Baby.

50:02.749 --> 50:03.583
Oh no, baby!

50:04.334 --> 50:05.585
Baby. Oh dear.

50:07.379 --> 50:09.631
Are you okay? My goodness.

50:10.298 --> 50:12.342
Just like that,
she's saved me time and again.

50:28.942 --> 50:30.193
Oh no!

50:34.614 --> 50:35.949
Oh no. Honey!

50:43.457 --> 50:45.625
-Are you okay?
-You better be a good daughter.

50:46.543 --> 50:49.755
What great person are you trying to be,
causing trouble so well?

50:50.464 --> 50:51.506
Will it leave a scar?

50:52.132 --> 50:55.177
You're worried about her scar?
She's lucky it wasn't worse.

50:55.260 --> 50:59.681
No one would believe it if you said
you caught a kid jumping off the roof.

50:59.765 --> 51:02.392
Mom, Dad.

51:02.476 --> 51:03.310
Oh dear.

51:05.479 --> 51:07.481
Why was she on the roof this time?

51:07.981 --> 51:10.358
She kept insisting she was a magpie.

51:16.239 --> 51:20.202
My little baby got stitches.
I can't even imagine how much it hurts.

51:21.578 --> 51:22.954
It was only much later,

51:23.622 --> 51:26.083
when I could no longer answer her calls,

51:26.792 --> 51:29.961
that I deeply missed her relentless worry.

51:30.670 --> 51:32.339
I'm so sorry.

51:33.924 --> 51:36.218
I'm sorry, baby. I'm sorry.

51:38.929 --> 51:39.763
It's okay.

51:41.098 --> 51:43.767
Her delicate heart sank countless times.

51:45.060 --> 51:47.395
I wish I'd shown her
a bit more appreciation.

51:49.106 --> 51:51.191
Regret arrived too late once again.

54:45.448 --> 54:50.453
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."

54:57.544 --> 54:59.921
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
